# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# The self-hosted fonts never change under a name (a new font gets a new file name), so phones keep them for a year
# instead of asking again on every page (wave 2026-10-26-ads S2). Way back: delete this file.
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Raptive is approved for recoverystarts.com only (2026-11-12, Code window raptive-install). Every branch and PR also gets
# a preview copy on *.pages.dev, and Raptive's head tag (which we may not change or wrap in a condition) would load ads
# there too. So on those hosts only, the browser may run inline scripts and our own files and nothing from elsewhere:
# Raptive's loader (and GA) never starts on a preview. recoverystarts.com and www get no new header from this.
# Checked in `wrangler pages dev` with Host headers. Way back: delete these four lines.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'

# Content-Language (2026-11-14, claude-home #514 / #489 step 6, deploy-1126): every page says the language its <html lang>
# says, the way the meeting map's pages already do (meeting-finder server/headers.mjs). Bing weighs this header over
# hreflang. English is everything; each /<code>/ folder detaches it and sets its own, because Pages joins two values of
# one header with a comma ("en, es") when two rules match (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# The codes are each folder's <html lang> exactly (pt is pt-BR); scripts/ci/site-check.js check 8 holds them together.
# Functions' answers (functions/) and the meeting map (the meetings Worker) don't read this file. Way back: delete
# from here to the end of the file.
/*
  Content-Language: en
/ar/*
  ! Content-Language
  Content-Language: ar
/de/*
  ! Content-Language
  Content-Language: de
/es/*
  ! Content-Language
  Content-Language: es
/fa/*
